parts+=['q-11536 and q-126009 have opaque compound banks. Their component projections above faithfully reproduce all original options and change with actual operands, but cannot establish the historical misconception. They are explicit evidence-only profiles at original and changed parameters. The q-126009 option containing the scalar b as a matrix entry is particularly underidentified. No opaque bank is a normal learning default. Other observed banks are also evidence-only for consistent fidelity/eligibility separation.','The default authored radio method bank is complete: C; reverse the matrix combine sign X∓Y; omit A scaling (A±Y); omit B scaling (X±B); omit the first scaled matrix (±Y). These are actual operations on the displayed method, with no unrelated offsets, random wrong values or inferred feedback. Bank count is five. A colliding whole bank rejects the entire instance. Blanks have no distractors.','## 4. Backbone and slots','Fixed: two supplied equally shaped matrices, two scalar products, ordered five-stage method, family add/subtract operator, field types/count, four requested scalar entries for blank families. The row family stays 1x4 and the rectangular family stays 2x3. Variable: matrix labels (distinct uppercase letters), all supplied entries, allowed nonzero scalar values, and four target-cell positions in the partial family. Labels/order are excluded from mathematical-task counts.','Easy: a,b∈{2,3}, A/B entries integers 0…4; nonzero matrices. Moderate: integer entries −6…6; half-plus a∈{2,…,6}, b=1/2 with even B; negative-plus a∈{−1,−2,−3}, b∈{2,…,6}; other square families a,b∈{2,…,6}; signed inputs required for their workload. Easy positive-only integer tasks cannot pass the moderate guard. Hard row: a∈{2,3,4}, b=1/2, even B, entries −6…6, subtraction. Hard rectangles: a∈{1/3,2/3}, b=2, A entries multiples of 3 bounded by 18, B integers/halves bounded by 6, giving integral scaled entries. Explicit inputs and samplers use these same bounds. These are conservative authored sampling policies, not recovered software ranges.','For q-320671 the source anchor targets are field-1→(1,1), field-2→(1,3), field-3→(2,2), field-4→(2,3); the other cells (1,2)/(2,1) are given. Pull order never determines cell position. The slot domain is all 15 four-cell subsets of six cells in row-major order: four requested cells and two supplied correct cells. Changing targets preserves the requested/given roles and four-entry assessment workload. Given values are computed from the actual supplied matrices. The changed-target regression holds scalars/matrices fixed and checks all fifteen masks, actual placeholder columns and answer keys.','Raw q-320671 source table staggers the bottom row by one Markdown column. Public observed replay preserves it exactly as ineligible evidence. Normal output inserts the missing bottom padding cell and removes the redundant trailing cell, placing both rows’ matrix entries in columns 3–5. This is a documented presentation repair, not a changed assessment. All original values/keys remain intact.','Raw q-11534/q-11536 retain missing difficulty, solution and correct refs; completed normal records infer only the uniquely correct mathematical matrix and author moderate assignment/solution. Raw q-11532 retains absent answer-fields; normal records author one five-choice radio field. Those inferred values are never counted as original designations. Canonical e-4382 lacks an A= assignment in its captured prompt; this is context evidence only, not a practice replay. Normal questions always name both supplied matrices.','Scope basis: lesson linked route follows first-step→next: Introduction; Multiplying a Matrix by a Scalar; Calculating the Value of a Scalar; Properties of Scalar Multiplication; this KP. The canonical example performs the same two scalar products then entrywise addition with a half scalar. Key prerequisite Evaluating Linear Expressions and topic predecessor Adding and Subtracting Matrices support the arithmetic. The scalar-solving sibling is a boundary, not a branch to add. Neither later matrix-column multiplication nor transpose/inverse topics is introduced.','Variety: level-capacity.json counts conservative valid subdomains separately from sampled uniqueness and target-slot coverage. Mathematical fingerprints contain the actual input matrices/scalars, response shape, and requested cells, excluding names, option order and bank profile. Content identity includes version, difficulty (or raw absence), actual prompt/solution, full displayed bank and field/reference presence; seeds/shuffling cannot change it.','Calculator flag remains unknown: the supplemental 86-record capture has no applicable flags. No calculator requirement is invented. All source anomalies and underidentified intent remain disclosed; no database operation or registration is prepared.']
